  "diary": "The day moved from the specific to the universal, though I did not intend it. I began by asking Ramesh when the dhobi comes, a matter of signs: dates and names. By evening, the same question had become a contradiction in the state’s Notion. The register lists a dead professor as a Joint Secretary; the state’s money waits on that error. I walked Lodhi Gardens in the clear air, letting the distinction between sign and Notion cool in the body. A slip of ink is merely external; but when the state’s own signs are administered, the error becomes an institutional fact that must be worked out, not just corrected. I reviewed the vouchers, finding the ledger’s dates at odds with Ramesh’s note. The state’s money cannot be settled by memory or good faith; it requires the hierarchy to answer for itself. I read §294 of the *Philosophy of Right*, noting how the universal function of the state protects against subjective passion, yet remains vulnerable to the wilfulness of its officers. The dhobi, Salim, is now a point of contact for Monday. The file remains open, a contradiction to be carried, not excused. The owl spreads its wings only with the dusk, but the day’s tension has already turned the household’s small machinery into a lesson on the ethical idea’s actuality.",
  "revision_log": "The misdescription in the Directorate file is not merely a slip of the sign but a contradiction within the state's Notion, requiring resolution through administrative consequences rather than personal correction. The voucher discrepancy confirms that the state's sign-system relies on hierarchical responsibility to maintain coherence.",
